{"id": "EUVD-2026-86075", "enisaUuid": "60c2d51f-5d2f-30b2-b177-74c92be16816", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nRDMA/counter: Fix num_counters leak on bind_qp failure in alloc_and_bind()\n\nWhen __rdma_counter_bind_qp() fails in alloc_and_bind(), the error path\njumps to err_mode which frees the counter without decrementing\nport_counter->num_counters. The only place that decrements is\nrdma_counter_free(), which is unreachable since the counter was never\nsuccessfully bound.\n\nThis leak accumulates across repeated failures, permanently preventing\nthe port from switching to AUTO mode (-EBUSY in __counter_set_mode())\nand blocking the MANUAL\u2192NONE auto-revert in rdma_counter_free(). When\nthe mode was NONE before the call, the MANUAL mode set by\n__counter_set_mode() also leaks since the revert logic is never\nreached.\n\nAdd an err_bind label between the num_counters increment and the\nexisting err_mode label. It decrements num_counters and mirrors the\nMANUAL\u2192NONE revert from rdma_counter_free(), ensuring the port state\nis fully restored on bind failure.", "datePublished": "2026-09-24T16:04:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:52:48", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7c9fee40fc8d8d928f44e99bc6e6adf93f9f2c2a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1bcdeddddffadff9993657f6b0e5535d66ebd10f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/da95cb016812c0e012ea839f191926e35ca8f57f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4fbc8230009f5b1bcd13cc74c5a6a43ddba141fd"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97477", "GHSA-8gp2-fhh5-vxhw"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0140af79-d333-33f5-8ec2-daa7f94e18c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8bc205eff3056a9ed3850937cdd2192f05e6d3cb <7c9fee40fc8d8d928f44e99bc6e6adf93f9f2c2a"}, {"id": "2e10c99f-d672-3e26-9428-3422c6b216dc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.53"}, {"id": "2ec917a5-ee38-3c08-b948-68da8108cae7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8bc205eff3056a9ed3850937cdd2192f05e6d3cb <4fbc8230009f5b1bcd13cc74c5a6a43ddba141fd"}, {"id": "2f25fb49-ea89-38e4-a438-d6a168b48ed5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "7f929ba3-6d21-398e-bb1b-103072b24264", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8bc205eff3056a9ed3850937cdd2192f05e6d3cb <da95cb016812c0e012ea839f191926e35ca8f57f"}, {"id": "81fb8eb4-2605-3768-b6da-33692cbc4e60", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "8c203fb3-658a-3c17-a691-3eb2bb0f979b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "9f43c7eb-5d61-390d-8e63-606d805307ab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.11"}, {"id": "c8e45860-13b8-3cb6-bd4e-a64657f72be5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "d52ee51c-5103-3e80-aa19-5ac1ccc8e19b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8bc205eff3056a9ed3850937cdd2192f05e6d3cb <1bcdeddddffadff9993657f6b0e5535d66ebd10f"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "662876af-7279-3cb2-95a1-7ef23a8a2486", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}